          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The Leray-Hirsch theorem states sufficient fiberwise condition for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            of the total space of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            of the base space.
          %p
            An important consequence is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p Let
          #eq:TheFiberBundles.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi F
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↪
                            %mi ι
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  F &amp;\stackrel{\iota}{\hookrightarrow}&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  }
          %p
            be an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            that admit the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
            of finite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
          %h3#StatementInOrdinaryCohomology In ordinary cohomology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(-;\,R)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+rings"} cohomology rings
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p If there exists
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
                of elements
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
